<title>BELGIUM: AEA's Jan-Apr cargo figures show overall gain.</title>
<headline>AEA's Jan-Apr cargo figures show overall gain.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The north Atlantic and Europe-sub-Saharan Africa routes were the only Association of European Airlines (AEA) regions to show a dip in Jan-Apr cargo flown from the first four months of last year but the global total was up 2.4 percent at 7,690 million revenue freight tonne kilometres (RFTK)</p>
<p>The statistics for Jan-Apr international scheduled services of AEA member airlines quoted in RFTK include:</p>
<p>    REGION			     JANUARY TO APRIL 1997</p>
<p>					   Million RTKF  Percent Change</p>
<p>							     Jan-Apr 1996</p>
<p>    Geographical Europe		316.8	 up   3.3</p>
<p>    Europe-N Africa/M East	   361.3	 up  11.8</p>
<p>    North Atlantic		   2,664.4     down   1.1</p>
<p>    Europe-Far East/Australasia  2,874.0	 up   4.3</p>
<p>    Europe-Sub Saharan Africa	603.7     down   3.8</p>
<p>    South Atlantic		     438.8	 up   5.7</p>
<p>    Mid Atlantic			 429.6	 up  12.5</p>
<p>    Total longhaul		   7,011.7	 up   2.0</p>
<p>    Total international	    7,689.8	 up   2.4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
